menu "WiCAN restart_tracker"

    config WICAN_RESTART_TRACKER_PARK_RETRY_MIN
        int "Crash park: start again by itself after this many minutes (0 = never)"
        range 0 1440
        default 0
        help
            After three runs in a row that crashed before they settled, the
            crash-loop brake parks the device asleep (README.md, "The
            crash-loop brake"). With 0 it stays parked until the power is
            cycled or the button is pressed. Any other value makes a parked
            device try one normal start after that many minutes, and park
            again at once when that start crashes too.

endmenu
